     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">You are absolutely right, there was a bug, which I just fixed on github. Thanks for catching that one! It would have been seriously problematic if it had made it into the release version. Glat it didn&#39;t thanks to you!<br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">2018-03-20 1:57 GMT+01:00 Travis Riddle <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">rid...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span>:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Paul,<div><br></div><div>I think I may have discovered a problem that can arise when specifying `by` variables in the grouping term. The short version is that it looks like when the identifying values contain periods, the levels get mixed up in estimation. Below is a reproducible example illustrating the issue:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\">#Data frame containing the &quot;person-level&quot; data</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>df  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ID </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">seq</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">200</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                  condition </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Treatment&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Control&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> each</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;A&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;B&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                  grp_mean </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">200</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#specify that the standard deviations vary by group</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>df_sd </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">condition</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Treatment&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Treatment&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Control&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Control&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;A&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;B&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;A&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;B&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                    grp_sd </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>df </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  left_join</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df_sd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  mutate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">grp_cond </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> paste</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> condition</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;_&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span 